{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1017","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. The Phone Number"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mrs. Smith is trying to contact her husband, John Smith, but she forgot the secret phone number!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only thing Mrs. Smith remembered was that any permutation of $$$n$$$ can be a secret phone number. Only those permutations that minimize secret value might be the phone of her husband."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The sequence of $$$n$$$ integers is called a permutation if it contains all integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ exactly once."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The secret value of a phone number is defined as the sum of the length of the longest increasing subsequence ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":") and length of the longest decreasing subsequence ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A subsequence $$$a_{i_1}, a_{i_2}, \\ldots, a_{i_k}$$$ where $$$1\\leq i_1 \\lt i_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt i_k\\leq n$$$ is called increasing if $$$a_{i_1} \\lt a_{i_2} \\lt a_{i_3} \\lt \\ldots \\lt a_{i_k}$$$. If $$$a_{i_1} \\gt a_{i_2} \\gt a_{i_3} \\gt \\ldots \\gt a_{i_k}$$$, a subsequence is called decreasing. An increasing/decreasing subsequence is called longest if it has maximum length among all increasing/decreasing subsequences."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if there is a permutation $$$[6, 4, 1, 7, 2, 3, 5]$$$, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of this permutation will be $$$[1, 2, 3, 5]$$$, so the length of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to $$$4$$$. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be $$$[6, 4, 1]$$$, $$$[6, 4, 2]$$$, or $$$[6, 4, 3]$$$, so the length of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note, the lengths of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be different."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So please help Mrs. Smith to find a permutation that gives a minimum sum of lengths of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$) — the length of permutation that you need to build."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a permutation that gives a minimum sum of lengths of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple answers, print any."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 4 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, you can build a permutation $$$[3, 4, 1, 2]$$$. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is $$$[3, 4]$$$ (or $$$[1, 2]$$$), so the length of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to $$$2$$$. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be ony of $$$[3, 1]$$$, $$$[4, 2]$$$, $$$[3, 2]$$$, or $$$[4, 1]$$$. The length of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is also equal to $$$2$$$. The sum is equal to $$$4$$$. Note that $$$[3, 4, 1, 2]$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the only permutation that is valid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, you can build a permutation $$$[2, 1]$$$. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is $$$[1]$$$ (or $$$[2]$$$), so the length of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LIS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to $$$1$$$. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is $$$[2, 1]$$$, so the length of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LDS"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to $$$2$$$. The sum is equal to $$$3$$$. Note that permutation $$$[1, 2]$$$ is also valid."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1017C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1017/problem/C"}